OL,3,GNEWSCCulture Secretary says "jury's    
OL,4,Cout" on Ofcom's ability to deliver     
OL,5,Conline safety role                     
OL,7,FCulture Secretary Lisa Nandy has       
OL,8,Fquestioned whether Ofcom is capable of 
OL,9,Fcarrying out the responsibilities the  
OL,10,Fgovernment has given it, in an         
OL,11,Finterview with Sky News broadcast      
OL,12,Ftoday.                                 
OL,14,FSpeaking to Sky's Cathy Newman, Nandy  
OL,15,Fsaid: "I think the jury's out about    
OL,16,Fwhether they can do what we've asked   
OL,17,Fthem to do."                           
OL,19,FSky News reported that she signalled   
OL,20,Fthe media regulator could be broken up,
OL,21,Fand that she said Ofcom needed to      
OL,22,F"shape up".                            
OL,23,EPub: 25-Nov-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
