OL,0,       GCEEFAX 1 145 Fri 27 NovC19:11/32
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G3/5 
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSCCulture Secretary says "jury's    
OL,4,Cout" on Ofcom's ability to deliver     
OL,5,Conline safety role                     
OL,7,FShe said she was actively discussing   
OL,8,Fthe matter with Ofcom's new chair, who 
OL,9,Fshe said had been brought in "to shake 
OL,10,Fthings up".                            
OL,12,FDespite indicating that a break-up was 
OL,13,Fpossible, Nandy said she would rather  
OL,14,Ftake a partnership approach, in which  
OL,15,Feveryone stepped up and recognised the 
OL,16,Furgency of the issue and their own     
OL,17,Fresponsibilities.                      
OL,23,EPub: 25-Nov-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
